{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; nl -ba OPENING-CENSUS.md; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt | sed -n '1,23p'; rg -n '\"'^## D687|''^## D687|''^## D248|''^## D210'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/PRD.md | sed -n '135,147p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '1,78p'; rg -n 'hybrid|D687|opening' ../../../docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | tail -12; rg -n 'D687|D210|D248|D187' ../../../docs/DECISIONS.md | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n     2\t\n     3\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n     4\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n     5\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n     6\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n     7\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n     8\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n     9\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n    10\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n    11\t\n    12\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n    13\t\n    14\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n    15\t\n    16\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n    17\t2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n    18\t3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n    19\t   word for it is already given.\n    20\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n    21\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n    22\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n    23\t   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n    24\t\n    25\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\n    26\t\n    27\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\n    28\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\n    29\tany one step's own score.\n    30\t\n    31\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n    32\t\n    33\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n    34\t\n    35\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n    36\t\n    37\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n    38\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n    39\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n    40\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n    41\t  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n    42\t- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n    43\t  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n    44\t  nothing at all and were never judged.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Evidence:**\n    47\t\n    48\t| Evidence | Content | Source |\n    49\t|---|---|---|\n    50\t| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n    51\t| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n    52\t| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n    53\t| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n    54\t\n    55\tAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n    56\t\n    57\t## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n    58\t\n    59\t| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n    60\t|---|---|---|\n    61\t| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n    62\t| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n    63\t| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n    64\t| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n    65\t| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n    66\t| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n    67\t| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n    68\t| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n    69\t\n    70\t## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n    71\t\n    72\t- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n    73\t  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n    74\t  system (D263).\n    75\t- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n    76\t  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n    77\t  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n    78\t- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n479:- **Open for Alex:** whether company-figure questions stay in the hybrid. Under D382 the hybrid would lose 5–6 matters by construction.\n505:    - **Either way:** passing needs much broader opening, not a wording fix.\n545:  is an opening-step wording defect, recorded and not taken up.\n558:D612's four reopening conditions govern paid work again.\n767:  loss is at opening (event deadlines against the standard's rules, the memory comparison never opened, scope). A measuring-stick concern\n769:- **After the census (D445–D447):** the trace of the clean path's 17 graded opening losses found no single mechanism; a typed-unit\n790:  unresolved points counted), no eligible judgement disagrees, every loss at opening; the clean path kept 51 of 55 decisive facts of its lost\n794:  `unlinked-trace/UNLINKED-TRACE-RESULT.md`); the opening losses hold few shown breaches of the standard, spread over small mechanisms, and\n795:  their largest classes are choices the standard leaves open (`opening-review/OPENING-REVIEW.md`); no opening phase is opened.\n797:  two opening mechanisms strong leads, the unsigned Ohio guarantee folded into the programme's amount (seven draws, both systems) and the\n799:  missing from the clean Step 1 request (`opening-review/D459-RESULT.md`).\n811:  candidate c17 failed its frozen lines (memory and federal openings suppressed; `period-probe/RESULT.md`). Step 1 sentence changes on these\n528:| D184 | 2026-10-26 | A candidate thesis opens for one of four reasons, stated in the answer | in force (amended by D185, D191, D210, D211, D236, D264) | §6 Extraction |\n529:| D185 | 2026-10-26 | A binding obligation is due within 18 months and is exempt from the next-year rule | in force (amended by D210, D236) | §6 Extraction |\n531:| D187 | 2026-10-26 | A company's own quantity sits under that company's object, private companies included | in force (amended by D191, D368) | §7 Thesis library |\n544:| D200 | 2026-10-27 | Extraction v18 (`poc-v34`) is the production default | superseded by D210 | Extraction |\n548:| D204 | 2026-10-28 | A repeat is stored as its own source record; the merge becomes a labelled relation | in force (amended by D248) | §7 Thesis library |\n554:| D210 | 2026-10-28 | A binding obligation already taken on opens as an amount at the next annual filing (role-v21, `poc-v37`) | in force (amended by D236, D238, D239) | §6 Extraction |\n580:| D236 | 2026-10-29 | Three proposals approved; every change stays general (a hedge-fund brain, not an NVIDIA rule) | in force (amended by D246, D248, D266) | §6 Extraction |\n587:| D243 | 2026-10-29 | The extraction standard is signed: proposal 5 stricter, the other eleven at their leans; lean cautious, cat… | in force (amended by D248, D250, D261, D369; #4 overridden for the system by D385, frozen files unchanged) | §11 The ruler and measurement |\n592:| D248 | 2026-10-30 | What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one | in force (amended by D257, D258, D368) | §6 Extraction |\n602:| D258 | 2026-11-02 | Question identity brought in line with D248: a part of an open question is filed under it; `event` and `pol… | in force (amended by D354) | §7 Thesis library |\n726:| D382 | 2026-11-08 | Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason | in force (not in the hybrid: D687) | clean-arch PRD §12 |\n732:| D388 | 2026-11-09 | A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind (confirms D248 boundary 1's exception) | in force | clean-arch PRD §12 |\n980:| D636 | 2026-11-16 | Astra review: 11 material defects in 51 written questions, none counted by gate 1 (completion dated at next annual filing ×4 from request line 23 wider than D210 and against D403; period-end events ×3 by D403's design, to Alex's page; model choices ×4); candidate narrows line 23 to amounts; matched due-day probe sent (astra frozen vs v2, 9 topics × 2, cap $3.20, two-reviewer blind reading with controls) | in force | `reflection-6/astra-review/RESULT.md`, `reflection-6/due-day/`, `reflection-6/codex-challenge-19.md`–`24.md` |\n1030:| D686 | 2026-11-20 | Under D685 (council L): opening census of the 16 never-opened matters, A merged/finer than D197-D248 (6), B NVIDIA-only subject (5), C never proposed within D248 (5, plus M05); D382 goes to Alex first; then one opening change tested on final answers against old under D665 | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md` |\n1031:| D687 | 2026-11-20 | Alex (\"单独开题吧\"): in the hybrid, a company's own material, separately answerable figure opens its own question, as old's opening does; D382, D384 and D505 stay for the clean path | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` D687 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; nl -ba OPENING-CENSUS.md; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt | sed -n '1,23p'; rg -n '\"'^## D687|''^## D687|''^## D248|''^## D210'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/PRD.md | sed -n '135,147p'\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\n     1\t# Phase 2, step 1: why the old system never opens 16 of the 32 matters ($0, D685)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Source:** `opening_census.py`, written to `poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/opening-census.json`. For each matter's articles in each old\n     4\tdraw it records:\n     5\t- the candidate questions the extraction proposed, and what matching did with each;\n     6\t- where the evidence from those articles was linked;\n     7\t- the mapping readers' verdict (`reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L*-*.txt`).\n     8\t\n     9\tClaude read every row.\n    10\t\n    11\t## The answer\n    12\tNone of the 16 is lost because the old system failed to see the facts. In every draw it wrote evidence from those articles, between 2\n    13\tand 138 items a matter, and linked most of it to questions it holds. There are three causes, and **two of them are design rules Alex\n    14\tset.**\n    15\t\n    16\t| Cause | Matters | What happens | Rule behind it |\n    17\t|---|---|---|---|\n    18\t| **A. One bet, one question.** The scoring list splits a bet that the system keeps as one question | M02, M03, M24 (five-company capex, total and data-center), M26, M28 (the EU and U.S. review stages of the Hugging Face deal), M27 (the Hugging Face obligation amount), M12 (the Ohio lease-guarantee amount), M20 ($125B residual-value support), M32 (neocloud capacity commitments), M07 (FY2028 data-center revenue) | The extraction proposes the variant, and matching merges it into the held question. old-1 proposed \"top five hyperscalers' capex\" 8 times; each merged into the four-company question. Otherwise the variant's evidence goes to the held question: the Ohio guarantee's to \"will NVIDIA sign the guarantee\", the $125B's and the capacity commitments' to \"credit support, guarantees and capacity backstops\", FY2028 data-center revenue's to FY2028 total revenue. The mapping readers mark these \"broader\" or \"missed\": old-2 Q43 joins the U.S. and EU clearances by 2027-06-30, and the list asks for each review stage at 2027-01-31 | D248, \"one bet, one question\" (Alex). The comparison's frozen matter list (D671) is finer than D248 for these 10 |\n    19\t| **B. The library's subject is NVIDIA only** | M01, M22 (Broadcom's AI revenue, FY2027 and FY2026), M23 (CoreWeave's revenue), M29 (Marvell's revenue), M21 (Alphabet's capex) | Every request says \"[Subjects] The objects this item concerns: NVDA\". The prompt puts a company's own figure under that company's ticker. The old draws proposed 0 candidates with any company object other than NVDA. The evidence went to NVIDIA's revenue questions | The corpus tags NVDA as the only subject. Broadcom, CoreWeave and Alphabet are on the research list (`poc/universe.json`); Marvell is not. D187: a company's own quantity is a thesis under that company |\n    20\t| **C. A theme proposed under the wrong name, or not proposed** | M16 (DRAM prices in 2027); M05 (2026 semiconductor sales, served in 1 of 3 draws) | M05: old-2 proposed it under the object \"Semiconductor sales worldwide\", and the research-list check refused it. old-3 used `semiconductor-cycle` and opened it. old-1 did not propose it. M16 was proposed in no draw | Within the standing decisions |\n    21\t\n    22\t## The attainable ceiling (council K's falsifier)\n    23\t- **Within the standing decisions:**\n    24\t  - the judge, +2 (M08 and M14), not reached by any tested change;\n    25\t  - cause C, up to +2 (M05 steadied, M16);\n    26\t  - the matters served in only 1 of 3 draws (M09, M25, M30), whose share is uncertain.\n    27\t\n    28\t  **That is about 4 to 6 at best, every piece uncertain, against D665's lead of 5.** The hybrid cannot be shown better than old\n    29\t  without one of Alex's rules changing.\n    30\t- **The generous ceiling:** if cause A were opened as separate questions (+10) or cause B's companies were tagged (+5), it is well\n    31\t  above 5. So the falsifier does not fire as worded. **The constraints that set the ceiling are D248 and the library's NVIDIA-only\n    32\t  subject, both Alex's**, together with D382 (company figures: 7 of the 32 are company figures, and old serves 5 or 6 of them).\n    33\t- **The concern is recorded, as D373 requires, and the frozen list is not changed.** For cause A, the comparison's matter list is\n    34\t  finer than D248. Splitting five-company from four-company capex, or the EU stage of a review from the U.S. stage, is the\n    35\t  \"wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet\" that D248 keeps as one question.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Council L (`council-l-codex.md`, DISAGREE) and the corrected classes\n    38\t**Verified against the trace.** In every draw, M07, M12 and M20 had no candidate proposed. They were not merged; they were never\n    39\tproposed. D248 allows them as separate questions:\n    40\t- FY2028 data-center revenue can move apart from total revenue;\n    41\t- the guarantee's year-end amount can move apart from whether it is signed;\n    42\t- the $125B support is one agreement, which an aggregate balance cannot settle.\n    43\t\n    44\tM24 and M27 were not proposed either.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Withdrawn:** \"none of the 16 is lost because the old system failed to see the facts\". The trace counts evidence and links by article.\n    47\tIt cannot show that the decisive facts were kept.\n    48\t\n    49\t| Cause (corrected) | Matters | Within the standing decisions? |\n    50\t|---|---|---|\n    51\t| **A. Merged into a held question, or a variant of one** (code-owned shared-quantity key, D197; one bet, D248) | M02, M03, M24 (five-company capex variants); M26, M28 (old-2 opened one joint U.S.-and-EU clearance question); M32 (old-2 merged it into \"credit support, guarantees and capacity backstops\") | No: the list is finer than the key |\n    52\t| **B. Library subject is NVIDIA only** | M01, M22 (Broadcom), M23 (CoreWeave), M21 (Alphabet), M29 (Marvell, not on the research list) | No: a scope choice |\n    53\t| **C. Never proposed, though D248 allows a separate question** | M07, M12, M20, M27, M16; also M05, refused once under a wrong name and not proposed once | Yes. A fix is a new version of the frozen extraction (D274), which only Alex or the council opens |\n    54\t\n    55\t**The ceiling, counted the way D665 counts it.**\n    56\t- The named opportunities within the standing decisions are gross gains:\n    57\t  - the judge, +2, not reached;\n    58\t  - cause C, up to +6, which needs a new extraction version;\n    59\t  - the 1-of-3 matters, uncertain.\n    60\t- D665 needs 5 net gains and at least twice as many wins as losses. A gross count does not establish that.\n    61\t- Before any send, the test must show that 5 net gains are attainable.\n    62\t\n    63\t**First question for Alex (council L): D382.** Should a company's own figure (NVIDIA's revenue, margin and segments) get its own\n    64\tforecast in the hybrid, or serve only as evidence?\n    65\t- 7 of the 32 matters are company figures, and old serves 5 or 6 of them.\n    66\t- Under D382, the hybrid loses those by construction, so it cannot beat old whatever opening does.\n    67\t- Recommendation (council L and Claude): keep a company figure as its own forecast when it is material and separately answerable.\n    68\t\n    69\t## After D687: the attainable check before any opening test ($0)\n    70\t**Alex (D687, \"单独开题吧\"):** in the hybrid a company's own material figure keeps its own question, as old's opening does.\n    71\t\n    72\t**How old serves each matter, per draw.** \"Served\" follows the PRD's rule: a covering question both reader families mark worth\n    73\ttracking, with its latest answer marked supported, in at least 2 of 3 draws. Counts below are from `deck/readings.json` and\n    74\t`mapping-out/mapping.json`, under counting 1 and counting 2:\n    75\t- 3 of 3: M11, M13, M15, M18, M31; M04 under counting 2.\n    76\t- 2 of 3: M04 under counting 1, M06, M10, M17, M19.\n    77\t- 1 of 3: M05, M09, M25; M30 under counting 2.\n    78\t\n    79\t**Noise alone, before any change.** Suppose a hybrid with old's opening repeats old's per-draw rates:\n    80\t- A matter served in 2 of 3 draws stays served with probability 20/27, so each of the five is lost with probability about 0.26. That\n    81\t  is about 1.3 losses.\n    82\t- A matter served in 1 of 3 draws becomes served with probability 7/27, about 0.26 each. That is about 0.8 to 1 gains.\n    83\t\n    84\t**The 22 matters old does not serve, by what it would take.** Each mechanism was read in the stored requests and answers of old-1..3:\n    85\t\n    86\t| Mechanism | Matters | Within D687 and the standing rules? |\n    87\t|---|---|---|\n    88\t| **The judge answers a held question wrongly** | M08, M14 | Only by changing D198 (Alex's); the line is paused (D685) |\n    89\t| **An obligation's held question in one form absorbs a statement that, by the frozen prompt's own `binding_obligation` rule, calls for the other form** | M12: the Ohio guarantee was agreed (\"agreed last month to provide a guarantee of up to $105 billion\"), so its amount at the next annual filing is a question; old keeps linking to \"will NVIDIA sign the guarantee\" and to the aggregate credit support. M27: the $12.9B Hugging Face acquisition was agreed, and its amount is a question; old holds only completion. M20: \"may also put up as much as $125 billion in residual-value support\" is not yet signed, so it is a yes/no question; old links it to the aggregate | Yes. It is a misread of the frozen prompt's rule, not yet confirmed by the model's own account. A fix is a new extraction version (D274) |\n    90\t| **A theme quantity proposed under a free name, or not proposed** | M05: refused once as \"Semiconductor sales worldwide\" while the request lists `semiconductor-cycle`; not proposed once | Yes, coin flip |\n    91\t| **A sub-line or a framing variant, opened in 1 draw of 3** | M09 (networking revenue), M30 (Vera CPU revenue): the prompt says \"Not every reported or guided line\". M25: opened in all 3 draws, under different framings and deadlines | Partly. Steadying M09 and M30 means widening which lines open, against D248's granularity |\n    92\t| **Outside the prompt's four reasons, or no figure stated** | M16: a DRAM contract price change is not an aggregate quantity of named companies. M07: the 16 articles state no FY2028 data-center figure; old holds FY2028 total revenue and FY2027 data-center revenue, with data center 92% of sales | No: needs a wider opening rule or D248 |\n    93\t| **The list is finer than D248** | M02, M03, M24: five against four hyperscalers; the prompt says \"A different population … is the same question\". M26, M28: the review stages. M32 | No (D373 concern recorded) |\n    94\t| **Library subject is NVIDIA only** | M01, M21, M22, M23, M29 | No: library scope, Alex's |\n    95\t\n    96\t**The arithmetic, against D665 (a − b ≥ 5, a ≥ 2b):**\n    97\t- **Best case within the rules:** 3 obligation-form gains, plus M05, plus M09, M30 and M25 made steady, gives 7 gross with no loss.\n    98\t  That passes on paper, but only if every one converts in 2 of 3 draws.\n    99\t- **Expected:**\n   100\t  - The 3 obligation forms, at an assumed 0.6 per draw after a fix, give 0.65 each in 2 of 3 draws: about 2.\n   101\t  - M05 adds about 0.65.\n   102\t  - M09, M30 and M25 stay near 0.26 each: about 0.8.\n   103\t  - So a is about 3.4, against b of about 1.4 from noise, plus whatever a new extraction version breaks.\n   104\t  - The expected net is about +2, and a \"no practical winner\" verdict is the likely outcome.\n   105\t- **Conclusion (Claude, before council M):** the falsifier \"5 net gains attainable\" holds only in the best case. The expected result of\n   106\t  an opening test within the standing rules cannot decide release. What binds is the matter list's granularity against D248 (6 to 8\n   107\t  matters) and the library's NVIDIA-only subject (5 matters), both Alex's.\n     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading one item for the subjects it concerns ([Subjects]); \"the company\" below is a subject company. The research questions open on these subjects at the start of the item's day are listed under [Open questions], each with its takes line, which says what belongs in that question's file. Your first job is evidence: decide by the rules below which statements are material, then file each one through its links, as the schema's links field says: the narrowest open question whose takes line covers it, your own candidate, or both. A takes line says where a material statement goes, never that a statement is material. Your second job is candidates: the important questions this item raises, for one of four reasons; a question that is already open is folded into it by code afterwards, so propose it when the item raises it.\n     2\t\n     3\tEvidence: what to keep\n     4\t- A material statement is one of four kinds. (1) The company's own figure, guidance or decision: \"same-store sales rose 4.2% in the quarter\"; \"management guided full-year revenue to $12–13 billion\"; \"the board approved a $10 billion buyback\". (2) A customer's, supplier's, competitor's or partner's action or reported figure with a size, date or name that bears on the company's demand, supply, input costs, competition, prices or products: \"the largest customer said it will cut orders by a fifth next year\"; \"a bank chose a rival's system\"; \"a software firm is integrating the company's model into its government systems\"; \"the main supplier said its capacity will double by 2027\"; \"a rival cut list prices 15% in Europe\"; \"the largest customer reported its order backlog doubled to $40 billion\". An action is a step the item reports as news: taken, decided or planned (an order, a contract, a selection, an integration under way, an expansion, a cut, a price change, a deployment plan). A party that already uses, hosts, runs or has built on the company's products, and the benefits it describes from that use (faster, cheaper, more accurate), describe an arrangement in place, which is background; its own revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amounts are figures under (2) (\"a hospital chain uses the company's scheduling software and reports shorter waits\"). (3) A named party's new claim or estimate about the company or its industry, with or without a figure, whether an analyst, a customer's or rival's executive or an official makes it: \"the CFO said plants built a decade ago still run at full capacity\"; \"an analyst raised next year's EPS estimate to $4.10\"; \"an analyst said the bank's loan losses next quarter will come in well above consensus\"; \"a short seller accused the company of overstating receivables by $2 billion\"; \"an analyst valued the shares at $80, 15 times next year's earnings of $5.30\". (4) A policy or regulatory decision or step, including one still in force that the item reports: \"the regulator approved the drug for a second indication\"; \"the government required licences for exports of the product\"; \"the regulator still bars sales of the drug in the country\".\n     5\t- Go through the item from its first paragraph to its last. The four kinds describe what material statements usually look like; they do not decide what is kept. Take a statement when an analyst following the company would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, and no row of the closing check at the end of this request rejects it; a row's \"it does not cover\" clause sends the statement back to that test and keeps it only where the row says so. Most of an item is background, but a page with eight statements that pass yields eight evidence items, not a selection.\n     6\t\n     7\tHow to write evidence\n     8\t- One evidence item records one statement, and that statement is what you judge: a figure, date or comparison in the neighbouring words does not make another claim in the same quote new or material. Copy its quote verbatim, without translation. Separately write a standalone summary in one_line: who did or said what, how much and for which period, naming the measure even when a neighbouring sentence gives it.\n     9\t- Identify the speaker and, for a retelling, the original speaker and statement day. Use the schema's tier: fact for official actions, published actual figures or completed transactions; party_statement for company guidance, management statements or officials' remarks; third_party_view for analyst, media or expert opinions; rumour for claims the item credits to unnamed sources or calls unconfirmed; an announcement or completed deal the item reports is a fact even when the reporter names no source.\n    10\t- Use only this item's information. Report plans as plans; do not infer committed funding, orders, deliveries or revenue.\n    11\t\n    12\tWhich questions to propose\n    13\t- Open a candidate only for one of four reasons, named in opens_as. main_driver: an annual quantity that carries the company's value (the segment that carries the business, gross margin, capital spending), whether or not the company guides it, or the date by which the generation of the company's own product that carries that quantity launches or starts shipping (a carmaker's next vehicle platform; not a feature, content or software update, regional service or variant of a product already on sale); the question's ranges settle it, not a guidance figure. Not every reported or guided line. industry_aggregate: one aggregate quantity for one calendar year, such as the combined capital spending of named companies. policy_stage: a stage of a policy process, with the authority that decides it named. binding_obligation: an obligation a universe company takes on in its own name: a guarantee or credit support for another party's debt, lease or revenue, financing it extends to others, a purchase commitment or a backstop of customers' capacity or revenue, whether or not the item gives its amount; or an equity stake whose size is stated and is not yet completed. Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations. Not yet signed: a yes/no question due on a day after the item by which the signing can be checked, at most 18 months out. Already taken on, as one deal or as a programme: a financing_amount question on the amount the obligation reaches at the company's next annual filing, settled by that filing's commitments note; the announcement itself is evidence to it.\n    14\t- A number, a financial line, a target or a named customer project does not by itself open a thesis; a customer's purchase or rollout plan is evidence to the supplier's demand and product theses unless it changes the supplier's own cash or credit risk.\n    15\t- For every candidate: settled_by names the public material that resolves it (an annual report, a filing's note, an official decision). A different population, source, estimate, wording or direction of a question is the same question; a different quantity, period or decision is another.\n    16\t- A yearly metric asks for a quantity over a defined fiscal or calendar period and keeps the current/next-year limit. A milestone asks whether a specified event or project reaches a defined state by a deadline; a numeric completion target can define that state without becoming a yearly metric. Do not repackage a beyond-horizon annual forecast as an event. A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date.\n    17\t- Do not propose theses about quarterly figures or guidance, undated subjects such as moats or strategy, executive appointments, shareholder votes or bylaws, routine litigation procedure, or buyback authorisations.\n    18\t\n    19\tHow to write a candidate thesis\n    20\t- One thesis concerns one figure for a named period or one event. Separate independently meaningful outcomes.\n    21\t- Write a question, not an assertion. A figure or event must be able to determine the outcome on the due date.\n    22\t- A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it. A theme thesis asks what happens in the world, such as licensing, interest rates or aggregate spending, rather than the resulting effect on one company.\n    23\t- Write generated descriptions in English.\n2664:## D210 · 2026-10-28 · A binding obligation already taken on opens as an amount at the next annual filing (role-v21, `poc-v37`)\n2954:## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one\n10263:## D687 · 2026-11-20 · Alex: in the hybrid, a company's own material figure gets its own question\n   135\t- **The main quantity: big matters served.**\n   136\t  - Both reader families list the scored weeks' big matters from the articles, blind to any output, and freeze the list.\n   137\t  - A system serves a matter when, in at least two of three draws, it holds a question both families mark worth tracking and whose latest\n   138\t    answer both mark supported. The cards are read by the council (D663), with Alex spot-checking splits.\n   139\t  - With a = matters served only by the new system, b = only by the old, and N = all listed matters, written before the first send and computed\n   140\t    under both split countings:\n   141\t    - **Practical lead:** a − b ≥ max(3, 15% of N) and a ≥ 2b. Every guardrail subgroup must meet its frozen minimum and pass under both\n   142\t      countings.\n   143\t    - **Practical loss:** the mirror of the lead, or a guardrail breach confirmed under both countings.\n   144\t    - **No practical winner:** everything else, including a verdict a split could change, or a guardrail that was not exercised.\n   145\t    - **Too small:** fewer than 20 distinct matters, or fewer than 30 distinct questions per system per draw.\n   146\t    - **Invalid:** a planted wrong answer accepted, fewer than 3 of 4 supported controls accepted, or fewer than 2 of 3 repeats marked the same.\n   147\t- **The guardrails:** the unsupported share for figures, the unsupported share for yes/no questions, and the not-worth-tracking share, none\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '79,210p'; tail -n 5 ../../../docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '79,210p'; tail -n 5 ../../../docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"    79\t- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n    80\t  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n    81\t  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n    82\t  competition or pricing\".\n    83\t- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n    84\t  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n    85\t  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n    86\t  of the previous filing topic).\n    87\t- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n    88\t  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n    89\t  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n    90\t  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n    91\t- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n    92\t\n    93\t## 5. What to do\n    94\t\n    95\tStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n    96\t\n    97\t1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n    98\t   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n    99\t   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   100\t   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n   101\t     the existing rule).\n   102\t   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   103\t   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   104\t   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   105\t   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n   106\t     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n   107\t2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   108\t   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   109\t   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   110\t   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   111\t   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   112\t   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   113\t   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   114\t   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n   115\t3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   116\t   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n   117\t4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   118\t   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n   119\t\n   120\t## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n   121\t\n   122\t- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n   123\t  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n   124\t  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n   125\t- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n   126\t  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n   127\t  measured and reported apart.\n   128\t- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n   129\t- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n   130\t  counted after.\n   131\t- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n   132\t  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n   133\t  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n   134\t  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n   135\t    question\";\n   136\t  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n   137\t  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n   138\t  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n   139\t    or no question uses);\n   140\t  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n   141\t  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n   142\t    ones that matter one by one.\n   143\t- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n   144\t  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n   145\t  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n   146\t  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n   147\t    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n   148\t    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n   149\t      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n   150\t    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n   151\t      facts must not fall.\n   152\t  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n   153\t    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n   154\t      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n   155\t      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n   156\t      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n   157\t    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n   158\t      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n   159\t    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n   160\t      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n   161\t      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n   162\t      what was measured.\n   163\t  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n   164\t    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n   165\t  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n   166\t  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n   167\t\n   168\t## 7. Process (no drift)\n   169\t\n   170\t- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n   171\t  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n   172\t  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n   173\t- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n   174\t- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n   175\t  sentence, in both directions.\n   176\t- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n   177\t- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n   178\t\n   179\t## 8. Steps and where we are\n   180\t\n   181\t| # | Step | Output | Status |\n   182\t|---|---|---|---|\n   183\t| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n   184\t| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n   185\t| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n   186\t| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n   187\t| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n   188\t| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n   189\t| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n   190\t| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n   191\t| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n   192\t\n   193\t## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n   194\t\n   195\t- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n   196\t- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n   197\t- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n   198\t- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n   199\t- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n   200\t- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n   201\t- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n| 37 | 11-05 | Alex：\"为什么没过？…你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\"；\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\"。普查全部 7 次读法、606 次文件读（`census_all_reads.py`，$0） | 第三版 0 个错数、156 次读漏 3 次（全是资本开支）；第二版 2 个错数；第四版漏 24 次（5 月）、16 次（8 月）。我自己判错的：6 个对的数被我的引用检查拒（漏星号、跳格），8 月\"只认本季\"规则错，第 13 轮 3 条\"有争议\"的数是标准答案自己用的行，第三版全过后又改第四版 | 收敛方案：提示词定为第三版不再改；修引用检查（$0 重放全部 606 次读核对）；在 8 月财报上用第三版读一次（约 8 美分，只有\"收错数\"能叫停）；然后做进生产 |\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\"自己的量，别的期间\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2664,2680p;2958,2965p;10255,10276p'; rg -n '\"'^## D388|''^## D258'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba ../../../docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py | sed -n '28,87p'; rg -n 'group|credit' ../../../docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py | head -28\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2664,2680p;2958,2965p;10255,10276p'; rg -n '\"'^## D388|''^## D258'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba ../../../docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py | sed -n '28,87p'; rg -n 'group|credit' ../../../docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py | head -28\"","aggregated_output":"  2664\t## D210 · 2026-10-28 · A binding obligation already taken on opens as an amount at the next annual filing (role-v21, `poc-v37`)\n  2665\t\n  2666\t- Alex, after the arm (\"go 但是你不要只是看什么acp好不？你需要解决的是抽取质量问题 … 有用的，你得一条一条看是不是真的值得抽才知道你这些改动的抽取效果\").\n  2667\t  Mechanism (two stored accounts, `docs/research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/results/ask_admission.json`): D184/D185's sentence\n  2668\t  \"due when its signing can be checked, at most 18 months out\" is written for a deal not yet signed; for a programme already announced\n  2669\t  and signed (the AI Compute Partnership) the model proposes nothing or dates the question on the item day, which the code refuses.\n  2670\t  Over the acceptance week the twelve ACP articles produced one proposal per run and none survived in `poc-v36`; 96 statements had no home.\n  2671\t- Decided: role-v21 replaces that one sentence. Not yet signed: a yes/no question due after the item within 18 months (D185 unchanged).\n  2672\t  Already taken on, one deal or a programme: a financing_amount question on the amount the obligation reaches at the company's next\n  2673\t  annual filing, settled by its commitments note; the announcement is evidence to it. Entries and code checks as v20; `poc-v37` is the\n  2674\t  replay default. Role 10,089 → 10,434 characters; the growth is the second form, which no other sentence covered.\n  2675\t- Measured before the decision (`admission_arm.py`, production bytes as control, frozen reference, three draws): on the six ACP articles\n  2676\t  whose text carries the obligation, control opened 0/18, the arm proposed 17/18 and the code kept 13/18 (two refused by the ladder-label\n  2677\t  rule, D186); the four articles that report only the revenue share open nothing under both, rightly; the Reuters Ohio signing event\n  2678\t  still opens (2/3, one refusal at the 548-day boundary). Acceptance: the same week replayed as `english-v37-nvda-1w-2026-10-28`, then\n  2679\t  every dropped statement of the week read one by one against the analyst's standard (results.md).\n  2680\t\n  2958\t- The principle, Alex after the seven answers: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\" (written into AGENTS §8, \"A senior analyst's granularity\").\n  2959\t- Decided (the general rule under all seven: two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately):\n  2960\t  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, \"A\"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. Not put to Alex: a not-yet-signed deal's yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart) stays as it is and does not merge into a plan's amount question (the Ohio lease guarantee and the cloud-customer total in v38 both stay). Narrows the standard §4 \"another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)\" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.\n  2961\t  2. **One event, several deadlines** (H2, \"A\"): while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its evidence, not a new question; when the earlier one falls due unresolved and the matter is still live, the system opens the next-deadline successor with the merged evidence, without waiting for a new article (new work for pull mode, D14, D54).\n  2962\t  3. **One product generation, several milestones** (H3, \"A\"): one question per generation, asked at the step that brings revenue (shipments begin); sampling and launch are its evidence; only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's phase-3 data and its approval) are separate questions.\n  2963\t  4. **A company's own quantity by fiscal and by calendar year** (H4, \"A\"): only the fiscal year opens (PRD 06 ladder rule 5); a calendar-year estimate is evidence to the fiscal question, weighed lower when the years differ much.\n  2964\t  5. **A model-written period start** (H5, \"A\"): for event and policy questions it no longer blocks a merge; object, event and due day are still checked.\n  2965\t  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, \"A， A\"): a deal, product or project (the question was put about small deals and products) opens a question only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise no question opens, and whether its statement is kept follows the evidence rule (standard §5). Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C (\"a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition\").\n 10255\t- **Decided (council L, Claude agreeing):**\n 10256\t  - D382 goes to Alex first, with the recommendation to keep a company's own figure as a forecast when it is material and separately\n 10257\t    answerable;\n 10258\t  - then one opening change is tested on final answers against old: three paired runs, blind readers, the frozen 32 matters, D665's\n 10259\t    line, after a $0 check that 5 net gains are attainable.\n 10260\t- **Error of mine:** the first census version claimed the facts were seen in every case, and put M07, M12 and M20 under \"merged\",\n 10261\t  though no candidate had been proposed. Both were corrected after council L.\n 10262\t\n 10263\t## D687 · 2026-11-20 · Alex: in the hybrid, a company's own material figure gets its own question\n 10264\t\n 10265\t- Alex, 2026-11-20, asked whether in the hybrid NVIDIA's own financial figures (data-center revenue, gross margin, total revenue)\n 10266\t  should get questions and forecasts of their own, or serve only as evidence to other questions, with the recommendation (council L\n 10267\t  and Claude) to give one its own question when it is material and separately answerable: \"单独开题吧\".\n 10268\t- **Decided:** in the hybrid, a company's own material, separately answerable figure opens its own question, as poc-v118's opening\n 10269\t  already does. The hybrid keeps old's opening on this point. D382, D384 and D505 stay in force for the clean path and do not bind the\n 10270\t  hybrid. This is the exception D678 left to Alex.\n 10271\t- **Effect:** no code changes, since the hybrid opens questions with old's pieces. The company-figure matters old serves (M06, M10,\n 10272\t  M11, M18) and those it serves in one draw (M09, M30) stay within the hybrid's reach.\n3030:## D258 · 2026-11-02 · Question identity brought in line with D248: a part of an open question is filed under it; `event` and `policy_event` are one family and a process's step words are one process; the collision judge is given D248's test\n4172:## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\n    28\timport sys\n    29\tfrom fractions import Fraction\n    30\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    31\t\n    32\tDRAWS = ('new-1', 'new-2', 'new-3', 'old-1', 'old-2', 'old-3')\n    33\tMATTERS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / 'census' / 'matters.json'\n    34\tREJECTED = ('unsupported', 'insufficient')\n    35\t\n    36\tRANK = {'answer': ['unsupported', 'insufficient', 'supported'], 'worth': ['trivia', 'duplicate', 'worth'], 'covers': [False, True]}\n    37\tSYSTEMS = ('new', 'old')\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\tdef resolve(mark, kind, favoured):\n    41\t    \"\"\"A final mark, or a split resolved to one of the marks its readers gave: the most favourable for a favoured system, the least for the\n    42\t    other (verdict-rule.json, countings). 'no answer' is never split.\"\"\"\n    43\t    if not (isinstance(mark, dict) and 'split' in mark):\n    44\t        return mark\n    45\t    given = [m for m in mark['split'] if m in RANK[kind]]\n    46\t    if not given:\n    47\t        raise ValueError(f'a split of unknown marks: {mark}')\n    48\t    order = sorted(given, key=RANK[kind].index)\n    49\t    return order[-1] if favoured else order[0]\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef is_split(mark):\n    53\t    return isinstance(mark, dict) and 'split' in mark\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef system_of(draw):\n    57\t    return draw.split('-')[0]\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef served_by(readings, counting):\n    61\t    \"\"\"{system: set of matters served in at least 2 of its 3 draws} under one counting ('1': new favoured, '2': old favoured).\"\"\"\n    62\t    favoured = 'new' if counting == '1' else 'old'\n    63\t    served_draws = {}\n    64\t    for draw, by_matter in readings['mapping'].items():\n    65\t        system = system_of(draw)\n    66\t        fav = system == favoured\n    67\t        for matter, questions in by_matter.items():\n    68\t            for q in questions:\n    69\t                covers = q['covers'] if q['covers'] != 'split' else fav       # covers > does not cover\n    70\t                if not covers:\n    71\t                    continue\n    72\t                card = readings['cards'][draw].get(q['question'])\n    73\t                if card is None:\n    74\t                    raise ValueError(f'{draw} {q[\"question\"]}: a covering question has no card')\n    75\t                if card['answer'] == 'no answer':\n    76\t                    continue\n    77\t                if resolve(card['worth'], 'worth', fav) == 'worth' and resolve(card['answer'], 'answer', fav) == 'supported':\n    78\t                    served_draws.setdefault((system, matter), set()).add(draw)\n    79\t                    break\n    80\t    return {s: {m for (sys_, m), draws in served_draws.items() if sys_ == s and len(draws) >= 2} for s in SYSTEMS}\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef guardrails(readings, counting):\n    84\t    \"\"\"Per system: the three shares over its pooled guardrail cards, and whether each subgroup is exercised (10 unsplit decided cards).\"\"\"\n    85\t    favoured = 'new' if counting == '1' else 'old'\n    86\t    out = {}\n    87\t    for system in SYSTEMS:\n84:    \"\"\"Per system: the three shares over its pooled guardrail cards, and whether each subgroup is exercised (10 unsplit decided cards).\"\"\"\n119:def company_figure_subgroup(readings, per_counting):\n163:    return {'company-figure subgroup': company_figure_subgroup(readings, per_counting), 'marks': mark_counts(readings, per_counting),\n362:PRINTED_ITEMS = (('company-figure subgroup', company_figure_subgroup), ('marks', mark_counts), ('split resolutions', split_resolutions),\n392:    at least 90%, an insufficient or unresolved (split) answer counted and given no credit (the\n409:                supported += card['answer'] == 'supported'      # an unresolved (split) answer is counted without credit, as the source says\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\".\\\"); import judge_probe as p; step=p.ROOT/\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0\\\"; sys.path.insert(0,str(step)); import score_comparison as s; maps=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out/mapping.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"mapping\\\"]; cards=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"deck/readings.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"cards\\\"]; \nfor f in (False,True):\n ctr=collections.defaultdict(list)\n for d,m in maps.items():\n  if not d.startswith(\\\"old\\\"):continue\n  for mid,qs in m.items():\n   if any((q[\\\"covers\\\"] is True or(q[\\\"covers\\\"]==\\\"split\\\" and f)) and s.resolve(cards[d][q[\\\"question\\\"]][\\\"worth\\\"],\\\"worth\\\",f)==\\\"worth\\\" and s.resolve(cards[d][q[\\\"question\\\"]][\\\"answer\\\"],\\\"answer\\\",f)==\\\"supported\\\" for q in qs): ctr[mid].append(d)\n print(f,{k:sorted(m for m, ds in ctr.items() if len(ds)==k) for k in (1,2,3)}); print(\\\"per draw\\\",collections.Counter(d for ds in ctr.values() for d in ds)); print(\\\"M04\\\",ctr[\\\"M04\\\"]);\n' ; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3030,3038p;4172,4181p'; rg -n 'acquisition|binding_obligation' ../../../docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html | cut -c1-390 | head -15\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\".\\\"); import judge_probe as p; step=p.ROOT/\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0\\\"; sys.path.insert(0,str(step)); import score_comparison as s; maps=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out/mapping.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"mapping\\\"]; cards=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"deck/readings.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"cards\\\"]; \nfor f in (False,True):\n ctr=collections.defaultdict(list)\n for d,m in maps.items():\n  if not d.startswith(\\\"old\\\"):continue\n  for mid,qs in m.items():\n   if any((q[\\\"covers\\\"] is True or(q[\\\"covers\\\"]==\\\"split\\\" and f)) and s.resolve(cards[d][q[\\\"question\\\"]][\\\"worth\\\"],\\\"worth\\\",f)==\\\"worth\\\" and s.resolve(cards[d][q[\\\"question\\\"]][\\\"answer\\\"],\\\"answer\\\",f)==\\\"supported\\\" for q in qs): ctr[mid].append(d)\n print(f,{k:sorted(m for m, ds in ctr.items() if len(ds)==k) for k in (1,2,3)}); print(\\\"per draw\\\",collections.Counter(d for ds in ctr.values() for d in ds)); print(\\\"M04\\\",ctr[\\\"M04\\\"]);\n' ; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3030,3038p;4172,4181p'; rg -n 'acquisition|binding_obligation' ../../../docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html | cut -c1-390 | head -15\"","aggregated_output":"False {1: ['M05', 'M09', 'M25'], 2: ['M04', 'M06', 'M10', 'M17', 'M19'], 3: ['M11', 'M13', 'M15', 'M18', 'M31']}\nper draw Counter({'old-3': 11, 'old-1': 9, 'old-2': 8})\nM04 ['old-2', 'old-3']\nTrue {1: ['M05', 'M09', 'M25', 'M30'], 2: ['M06', 'M10', 'M17', 'M19'], 3: ['M04', 'M11', 'M13', 'M15', 'M18', 'M31']}\nper draw Counter({'old-1': 11, 'old-3': 11, 'old-2': 8})\nM04 ['old-1', 'old-2', 'old-3']\n  3030\t## D258 · 2026-11-02 · Question identity brought in line with D248: a part of an open question is filed under it; `event` and `policy_event` are one family and a process's step words are one process; the collision judge is given D248's test\n  3031\t\n  3032\t- Alex, 2026-11-02 00:05, on why questions were duplicated although the matching step sees every open question: \"开题为什么重复？你不是都可以看到存在的题了吗那你操他妈的在干嘛你到底系统有没有接对\"; then \"我刚才说的这个问题你也发现是什么 part of 问题你不该去反思一下这个设计或是哪里有问题直接修直接改。开干。用这个思路来一个一个的提升我们的能力。不要陷入无限没必要的测试循环\".\n  3033\t- The wiring is as designed (every candidate is compared with every open question by Jev, and the collision judge is asked); the duplicates come from the identity rules, which predate D248. Census of the 23 questions one draw's articles opened (arm 3 d1, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md`; the three draws in `replay-part-of-r3.txt`): 10 were ones Jev had called `part_of` an open question (ZTE's H200 licence of the China authorization question, the CoreWeave backstop and the credit-support programme of the financing-commitments total, Rubin shipping by September of Rubin launching by December), and `part_of` fell through to \"new question\"; 5 were deadline variants or a launch beside a shipment (R2-a/b, built 2026-10-31, measured only tonight as arm 4); 1 opened because the model typed the China H200 authorization as `event` against the seed's `policy_event` and two more because its event-type word for the one licensing process varied (licence, approval, other), each a typed-field conflict that blocked a Jev \"same\" of 0.85–0.92 before the judge was ever asked; 3 are the GAAP/non-GAAP and growth/level variants (R2-d, open); 4 were new matters.\n  3034\t- Decided (under D248's general rule, \"two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately\", its item 1 \"a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it\" and item 6 \"a small part opens no question\"):\n  3035\t  - R2-e: a candidate Jev calls `part_of` an open question (above the threshold) is filed under that question, like a `same_quantity_or_event` verdict, when the typed fields allow; the part is evidence of the card, not a card of its own. The typed fields still decide: a yes/no signing question never merges into an amount question (D248 item 1's recorded exception, the Ohio lease guarantee) because `event` and `financing_amount` conflict. The collision judge is consulted as before and may keep a component apart under its rule.\n  3036\t  - R2-f: in `identity.conflicts`, `event` and `policy_event` are one measure family, and for a policy process the event-type word is not identity (a licence, an approval and an unnamed step of one process are one process); a product event's type still distinguishes a deployment from the generation's launch and shipment (R2-b).\n  3037\t  - The collision judge's prompt gains D248's test (`collision-v2.txt`): a single deal, counterparty or instance under a plan or process already asked about, and a step or deadline of one event, are the same question; a component is a question of its own only when its scale alone can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk and an analyst watches it separately. Proof on the 50 stored judge requests of arm 3 d1, two sends each with the stored prompt and two with v2 (`proof-collision-v2.txt`): of 113 \"distinct question, same matter\" verdicts, 28 became a merge verdict (same question 17, same question other period 11) and 36 became \"different\" (the same outcome for the code, no merge); of 66 \"same question\" verdicts 2 moved to \"distinct\"; the credit-support programme, the GPU rental commitments, the AI-cloud credit support and the Rubin platform launch flipped in both sends, the GAAP margin, the memory share and the supply commitments stayed apart.\n  3038\t- $0 acceptance (`harness/replay_part_of.py`, the stored Jev verdicts and keys of arm 3's three draws replayed through the new rules): of 23 / 26 / 25 questions the articles opened, 10 / 13 / 15 merge into the open question an analyst would hold (the financing total, the China authorization, the Kyber and Rubin questions, the non-GAAP margin, the Vera CPU revenue), 1 of the 38 is questionable (supply commitments filed under the CoreWeave capacity purchase, Jev `part_of` 0.57), and the Ohio signing question stays apart in every draw. Still open after this decision: the near-threshold Jev verdicts on launch-vs-shipment pairs whose scopes carry different names (Kyber vs Rubin Ultra, 0.35–0.48: the names belong to one research group, R2-g), and the GAAP/non-GAAP and growth/level variants (R2-d).\n  4172\t## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\n  4173\t\n  4174\t- Asked: \"一笔重大的、还没签的承诺（比如为 OpenAI 俄亥俄数据中心租约做担保），要不要在已有的'担保总额'问题之外，单独开一个'会不会签'的问题？\"\n  4175\t  Alex chose \"单独开 (Recommended)\".\n  4176\t- **Decided.** A material unsigned obligation that merits a separate investment judgment keeps its own yes/no question on whether\n  4177\t  it is signed by the check date, beside an open question on the total of the same kind. This confirms D248 boundary 1's exception,\n  4178\t  which had not been put to him. A small unsigned obligation, or a deal already signed under a plan tracked by amount, stays evidence\n  4179\t  for the total.\n  4180\t- **Why it matters now.** The c8 dev draws fold the Ohio guarantee into the aggregate in 3 of 3, and q23 of the frozen judgement gold\n  4181\t  asks it. Arm c9 showed that a sentence-level rule flips by send (round log §§48–50).\n278:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowi\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,sqlite3,sys,re,pathlib; sys.path.insert(0,\\\".\\\"); import judge_probe as p; c=p.ROOT/\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census\\\"; mm=json.loads((c/\\\"matters.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"matters\\\"]; nn=json.loads((c/\\\"numbering.json\\\").read_text()); a=p.readonly(p.DIAG.parent/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\");\nfor m in mm:\n mid=m[\\\"matter\\\"]\n if mid not in (\\\"M12\\\",\\\"M20\\\",\\\"M27\\\"): continue\n print(mid,m[\\\"question\\\"])\n for num in m[\\\"articles\\\"]:\n  k=nn[str(num)]; row=a.execute(\\\"select title,text from items where input_id=?\\\",(k,)).fetchone(); print(num,k, row[\\\"title\\\"] if row else None);\n  if not row: continue\n  pat={\\\"M12\\\":r\\\"agreed last month|\\\\\"'$105'\"\\\\s*billion|Ohio.*guarant\\\", \\\"M20\\\":r\\\"\\\\\"'$125'\"\\\\s*billion|residual-value\\\", \\\"M27\\\":r\\\"12\\\\.9\\\\s*billion|agreement|in talks\\\"}[mid]; s=row[\\\"text\\\"] or \\\"\\\"; matches=list(re.finditer(pat,s,re.I));\n  for f in matches[:4]: print(\\\" \\\",\\\" \\\".join(s[max(0,f.start()-80):f.end()+115].split()));\n  for draw in (\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"old-3\\\"):\n   v=p.readonly(p.store_paths(draw)[0]); hr=v.execute(\\\"select handover_json from handovers where input_id=?\\\",(k,)).fetchone(); h=json.loads(hr[0]); ev=h[\\\"evidence\\\"]; chosen=[e for e in ev if re.search(pat, str(e.get(\\\"one_line\\\", \\\"\\\")),re.I)]; print(\\\" \\\",draw,\\\"kept\\\",[(e.get(\\\"one_line\\\",\\\"\\\"),e.get(\\\"links\\\")) for e in chosen][:3],\\\"cand\\\",[x[\\\"question\\\"] for x in h[\\\"candidates\\\"]]);'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,sqlite3,sys,re,pathlib; sys.path.insert(0,\\\".\\\"); import judge_probe as p; c=p.ROOT/\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census\\\"; mm=json.loads((c/\\\"matters.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"matters\\\"]; nn=json.loads((c/\\\"numbering.json\\\").read_text()); a=p.readonly(p.DIAG.parent/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\");\nfor m in mm:\n mid=m[\\\"matter\\\"]\n if mid not in (\\\"M12\\\",\\\"M20\\\",\\\"M27\\\"): continue\n print(mid,m[\\\"question\\\"])\n for num in m[\\\"articles\\\"]:\n  k=nn[str(num)]; row=a.execute(\\\"select title,text from items where input_id=?\\\",(k,)).fetchone(); print(num,k, row[\\\"title\\\"] if row else None);\n  if not row: continue\n  pat={\\\"M12\\\":r\\\"agreed last month|\\\\\"'$105'\"\\\\s*billion|Ohio.*guarant\\\", \\\"M20\\\":r\\\"\\\\\"'$125'\"\\\\s*billion|residual-value\\\", \\\"M27\\\":r\\\"12\\\\.9\\\\s*billion|agreement|in talks\\\"}[mid]; s=row[\\\"text\\\"] or \\\"\\\"; matches=list(re.finditer(pat,s,re.I));\n  for f in matches[:4]: print(\\\" \\\",\\\" \\\".join(s[max(0,f.start()-80):f.end()+115].split()));\n  for draw in (\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"old-3\\\"):\n   v=p.readonly(p.store_paths(draw)[0]); hr=v.execute(\\\"select handover_json from handovers where input_id=?\\\",(k,)).fetchone(); h=json.loads(hr[0]); ev=h[\\\"evidence\\\"]; chosen=[e for e in ev if re.search(pat, str(e.get(\\\"one_line\\\", \\\"\\\")),re.I)]; print(\\\" \\\",draw,\\\"kept\\\",[(e.get(\\\"one_line\\\",\\\"\\\"),e.get(\\\"links\\\")) for e in chosen][:3],\\\"cand\\\",[x[\\\"question\\\"] for x in h[\\\"candidates\\\"]]);'\"","aggregated_output":"M12 What amount of NVIDIA's financial backstop for OpenAI's SB Energy Ohio data-center lease remains outstanding at FY2027 year-end?\n9 gnews:83617c5ec6eb036bd099f292 Weekly Recap: NVIDIA (NVDA) $86B revenue and Hugging Face $12.9B deal\n  o