instance, the company agreed last month to provide a guarantee of up to $105 billion for a massive data center in Ohio that will be leased to OpenAI, with\n  ts. For instance, the company agreed last month to provide a guarantee of up to $105 billion for a massive data center in Ohio that will be leased to OpenAI, with payments by Nvidia set to trigger in case th\n  old-1 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of lease payments for an Ohio data center to be leased to OpenAI, with payments triggered by OpenAI defaulting or failing to pay rent.', ['v1', 'v2', 'v19', 'v24'])] cand []\n  old-2 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion for an Ohio data center leased to OpenAI, with payments triggered if OpenAI defaulted on or failed to make lease payments.', ['v2', 'v3', 'v22'])] cand []\n  old-3 kept [('NVIDIA agreed last month to guarantee up to $105 billion for an Ohio data center leased to OpenAI, with payments triggered if OpenAI defaulted on or failed to make lease payments.', ['v1', 'v2', 'v21'])] cand []\nM20 Will NVIDIA sign residual-value support agreements (up to $125B) for the Goldman Sachs/Blackstone AI infrastructure partnerships by 2027-03-31 (researcher-set check date)?\n322 gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 Analysis: What Nvidia’s Massive Supply-Demand Gap Says About AI Mania\n  and Exchange Commission. The AI infrastructure giant may also put up as much as $125 billion in “residual-value support” for partnerships with several Wall Street heavyweights, including Goldman Sachs and Bl\n  ission. The AI infrastructure giant may also put up as much as $125 billion in “residual-value support” for partnerships with several Wall Street heavyweights, including Goldman Sachs and Blackstone, which pla\n  old-1 kept [('CRN reported that NVIDIA may provide up to $125 billion of residual-value support for partnerships with Goldman Sachs, Blackstone, and other financial firms planning to pool $500 billion for AI-infrastructure purchases.', ['v2', 'v29'])] cand []\n  old-2 kept [('CRN reported that NVIDIA may provide up to $125 billion in residual-value support for partnerships involving Goldman Sachs and Blackstone, which plan to pool $500 billion for AI-infrastructure purchases.', ['v2'])] cand []\n  old-3 kept [('CRN reported that NVIDIA may provide up to $125 billion of residual-value support for partnerships with Goldman Sachs, Blackstone and other firms planning to pool $500 billion for AI infrastructure purchases.', ['v1'])] cand []\nM27 How much of NVIDIA's agreed Hugging Face acquisition obligation remains outstanding at FY2027 year-end?\n3 gnews:614f5923f678d9e3ed34147b 'The planets aligned': Nvidia confirms $12.9bn Hugging Face deal in potentially huge AI shake-up\n  otentially huge AI shake-up By Craig Hale Hugging Face snapped up by Nvidia in $12.9 billion deal Nvidia pays $11.9 billion for Hugging Face, and a further $1 billion in equity-based retention The company pr\n  rted open weight models Nvidia has confirmed plans to acquire Hugging Face for $12.9 billion subject to regulatory approval, marking a major expansion for the chipmaker as it snaps up one of the most importa\n  uisition, and if it closes, it'll be Nvidia's biggest acquisition to date. The $12.9 billion payout comprises a Hugging Face valuation of $11.9 billion (way above its earlier $4.5 billion valuation in 2023)\n  old-1 kept [('NVIDIA confirmed plans to acquire Hugging Face for $12.9 billion, subject to regulatory approval.', ['v35'])] cand []\n  old-2 kept [('NVIDIA confirmed plans to acquire Hugging Face for $12.9 billion, subject to regulatory approval.', ['v34'])] cand []\n  old-3 kept [('NVIDIA confirmed plans to acquire Hugging Face for $12.9 billion, subject to regulatory approval.', ['v39']), ('The reported $12.9 billion acquisition price comprises an $11.9 billion valuation for Hugging Face and around $1 billion for an equity-based retention program.', ['v39'])] cand []\n9 gnews:83617c5ec6eb036bd099f292 Weekly Recap: NVIDIA (NVDA) $86B revenue and Hugging Face $12.9B deal\n  old-1 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion; the deal requires regulatory approval and is targeted to close in the first half of 2027.', ['v35'])] cand []\n  old-2 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for about $12.9 billion; the deal requires regulatory approval and is targeted to close in the first half of 2027.', ['v34'])] cand []\n  old-3 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for about $12.9 billion, subject to regulatory approval, with a planned close in the first half of 2027.', ['v39'])] cand []\n20 gnews:de07c33be81c960f8d6543be Jim Cramer Discusses NVIDIA (NVDA) Acquiring Hugging Face\n  ing Face Acquisition and Inference Expansion NVIDIA Corporation's (NASDAQ:NVDA) agreement to acquire open-source platform Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion represents a significant strategic sh\n  NVDA) agreement to acquire open-source platform Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion represents a significant strategic shift deeper into the software deployment ecosystem. By acquiring one of the le\n  old-1 kept [('The article reported that NVIDIA had agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion; it described the transaction as proposed.', ['v35'])] cand []\n  old-2 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion; the item gives no agreement date.', ['v34'])] cand []\n  old-3 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion; the agreement was reported on September 7, 2026.', ['v39'])] cand []\n277 gnews:c241264df3727d1416ad46e8 What Is Hugging Face, Nvidia's Latest Acquisition?\n  ecent announcement that Nvidia agreed to acquire the company Hugging Face . The agreement was made public on September 2, 2026, and the $12.9 billion deal, set to finalize in the first half of 2027, bring\n  any Hugging Face . The agreement was made public on September 2, 2026, and the $12.9 billion deal, set to finalize in the first half of 2027, brings one of the most prominent figureheads in open AI developme\n  old-1 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for $12.9 billion; the deal was announced September 2, 2026, and is set to finalize in the first half of 2027.', ['v35', 'c1'])] cand ['Will NVIDIA complete its acquisition of Hugging Face by June 30, 2027?']\n  old-2 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face in a $12.9 billion deal made public September 2, 2026, with finalization planned for the first half of 2027.', ['v34'])] cand []\n  old-3 kept [('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face in a $12.9 billion deal, announced September 2, 2026, with closing expected in the first half of 2027.', ['v39'])] cand []\n398 gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8 NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection\n  nounced it will acquire open-source AI platform Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion (¥2 trillion). Hugging Face CEO Clément Delangue, who had rejected a roughly $500 million investment from NVIDIA i\n  will acquire U.S.-based open-source AI platform Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion (¥2 trillion). A definitive agreement was signed on September 2, 2026, and CEO Jensen Huang disclosed the deal in\n  atform Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion (¥2 trillion). A definitive agreement was signed on September 2, 2026, and CEO Jensen Huang disclosed the deal in an official blog post on September 3.\n  maintaining momentum for open models. From Investment Rejection to Acquisition Agreement Hugging Face is a platform for publishing and sharing AI models, datasets, and applications. If Google's Google Do\n  old-1 kept [('NVIDIA signed a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face on September 2, 2026; Jensen Huang disclosed the deal on September 3, with completion targeted for the first half of 2027 subject to regulatory approvals in multiple jurisdictions, including the EU.', ['v35', 'v47']), (\"The article estimates Hugging Face annualized revenue at approximately $150 million and calculates NVIDIA's $12.9 billion acquisition price at roughly 86 times price-to-sales.\", ['v35', 'v47'])] cand []\n  old-2 kept [('NVIDIA signed a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face on September 2, 2026; Jensen Huang disclosed the deal on September 3.', ['v34', 'c1']), ('NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion.', ['v34', 'c1']), ('Jensen Huang said $12.9 billion was necessary to secure the Hugging Face deal amid competing bidders, and denied bidding to keep it from a competitor.', ['v34'])] cand [\"Will the required U.S. and EU regulatory reviews of NVIDIA's Hugging Face acquisition be cleared by 2027-06-30?\"]\n  old-3 kept [('NVIDIA announced its planned acquisition of Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion; the companies signed a definitive agreement on September 2, 2026, and Jensen Huang disclosed it on September 3.', ['v39']), (\"The article estimates Hugging Face annualized revenue at approximately $150 million, implying NVIDIA's $12.9 billion acquisition price is about 86 times annualized sales.\", ['v39'])] cand []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html | sed -n '269,287p'; rg -n '\"'^## D(236|184|191|239)'\"\\\\b' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n -i 'floor.*theme|market.*price' ../../../docs/prd/06-views.md | head -10; nl -ba ../../../docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '1,32p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html | sed -n '269,287p'; rg -n '\"'^## D(236|184|191|239)'\"\\\\b' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n -i 'floor.*theme|market.*price' ../../../docs/prd/06-views.md | head -10; nl -ba ../../../docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '1,32p'\"","aggregated_output":"   269\t<p><b>不进账本的：</b>归档找不到家的证据，记 <code>no home</code> 扔掉<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。评估时逐条读被扔的，分四种：抽取的垃圾；库里缺这个问题（覆盖缺口）；问题在却没挂上（归档错）；该开没开（开题错）。各归各的环节<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §7</span>。存储的表结构归 PRD 06 管。</p>\n   270\t\n   271\t<h2 id=\"types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类：账本的几大类型</h2>\n   272\t<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n   273\t<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n   274\t<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n   275\t<tbody>\n   276\t<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n   277\t<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n   278\t<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n   279\t<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n   280\t<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n   281\t</tbody></table></div>\n   282\t\n   283\t<p>例子（跨行业）：</p>\n   284\t<ul>\n   285\t<li><b>A：</b>NVIDIA FY2027 数据中心收入；一家地区银行 FY2026 净利息收入；一家公用事业公司 2027 年费率基数。</li>\n   286\t<li><b>B：</b>下一代机架系统能否在 2027 年底前开始出货；一家车企的新平台能否在 2026 年内开始交付。</li>\n   287\t<li><b>C：</b>NVIDIA 为云客户产能兜底的义务在 FY2027 年报达到多少；一家保险公司是否在 2027 年中前为合资公司 5 亿美元债务签署担保。</li>\n2464:## D184 · 2026-10-26 · A candidate thesis opens for one of four reasons, stated in the answer\n2503:## D191 · 2026-10-26 · Theme theses reach every company; no named dependant is required to open one\n2869:## D236 · 2026-10-29 · Three proposals approved; every change stays general (a hedge-fund brain, not an NVIDIA rule)\n2888:## D239 · 2026-10-29 · role-v29 (`poc-v45`) is the extraction request; the bench loop stops\n     1\t# Current state\n     2\t\n     3\t**Clean Steps 1–3, current (2026-11-11).** Records: Step 1, [round log](../clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md) §§16–47; Step 2, [Step 2 log](../clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md) §§12–19.\n     4\t- **Step 1 configuration: c8, adopted by Alex (D387).** It runs DeepSeek Flash at high effort, with a 64,000-token output cap; a\n     5\t  format failure or a cut answer is resent once (D380). It carries Alex's decisions D382–D385:\n     6\t  - figures are conditions;\n     7\t  - material statements with no thesis are kept without links;\n     8\t  - only big matters open a thesis;\n     9\t  - no target prices.\n    10\t\n    11\t  [PRD §12](../clean-arch/PRD.md) holds its system prompt, closing check and schema; a run with no candidate files sends exactly the\n    12\t  accepted request.\n    13\t- **Acceptance (D386, [protocol](../clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/ACCEPTANCE-PROTOCOL.md)).** 50 fresh articles that no run,\n    14\t  old or new, had used: news from 2026-09-05 to 09-07, a holiday weekend with no NVIDIA posts. One draw; two readers and a third on\n    15\t  disputes.\n    16\t  - helpful 132/139 (core 83/83);\n    17\t  - wrongly opened theses 1 of 10;\n    18\t  - search 141/143 available repeat pairs, or 141/145 for the whole system (one 11-article story supplies 55 pairs, and revisions are\n    19\t    barely exercised);\n    20\t  - clear wrong merges 1/57, plus 2 overlaps;\n    21\t  - detail retention 22 = 22. This is a storage comparison: every record keeps its own text. It is not a usability test.\n    22\t\n    23\t  Dev ×3 on the frozen golden-v5 (a lead): helpful 214, 211 and 212 of 234; search 98.9–100%; clear wrong merges about 1%. Step 1\n    24\t  cost for the fresh set plus dev ×3: $4.20 at published rates.\n    25\t- **Steps 2 and 3** are built in isolation (`clean-arch/step2`, `clean-arch/step3`): search, comparison, grouping and later linking.\n    26\t  They are not integrated with production storage. **Step 4 (judging) has not passed** on the clean path: its ladder step is built and\n    27\t  measured (four Stage A runs, lines missed by 1 to 3 answers; D426), so nothing yet shows the clean system can judge an investment\n    28\t  view on its own questions.\n    29\t- **Step 2 is closed and frozen (Alex, D427, 2026-11-11;** [Step 2 log](../clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md) §§14–19**).** It goes\n    30\t  to production only with the whole clean path, after Step 4 meets its lines; `tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py` guards its files. Its three lines were met at the acceptance above (one draw; \"later version\"\n    31\t  relations barely exercised), and no miss of the seeded end-to-end test (clean 18, 18, 17 against production 17, 15, 16) has\n    32\t  been traced to it (the two single-draw misses were diagnosed on 2026-11-11, below: neither traces to Step 2). What happened since the close-out of 2026-11-08:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,re,sys; sys.path.insert(0,\\\".\\\"); import judge_probe as p; c=p.ROOT/\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census\\\"; ms=json.loads((c/\\\"matters.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"matters\\\"]; nn=json.loads((c/\\\"numbering.json\\\").read_text()); a=p.readonly(p.DIAG.parent/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\");\nfor m in ms:\n if m[\\\"matter\\\"] not in (\\\"M16\\\",\\\"M07\\\"): continue\n print(m[\\\"matter\\\"],m[\\\"articles\\\"]);\n for num in m[\\\"articles\\\"]:\n  i=nn[str(num)]; u=a.execute(\\\"select title,text from items where input_id=?\\\",(i,)).fetchone(); s=\\\" \\\".join((u[\\\"text\\\"] or \\\"\\\").split()); pat=r\\\"(?:DRAM|memory).{0,75}(?:contract pric|2027)|2027.{0,80}(?:memory|DRAM)\\\" if m[\\\"matter\\\"]==\\\"M16\\\" else r\\\"(?:Data Center|data-center|Data Centre).{0,75}(?:FY2028|fiscal 2028)|(?:FY2028|fiscal 2028).{0,75}(?:Data Center|data-center|Data Centre)\\\"; match=list(re.finditer(pat,s,re.I));\n  if match:\n   x=match[0]; print(num,u[\\\"title\\\"],s[max(0,x.start()-35):x.end()+105])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
